                <pb facs="1265" n="1115" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1115"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister
                    Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Department is advised of the Belgian assent conditional on unanimity of Hague
                    signatories. Delay on part of China may cause embarrassment. Mr. Rockhill is
                    directed to request Chinese Government to cable assent promptly to Russian
                    Government and notify the Government of the Netherlands that it has done
                    so.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
